language "law.core" version "0.2";
package examples.fr.code_civil.imprevision_force_majeure version "0.1.0";
namespace "urn:law:examples:fr:code-civil:imprevision-force-majeure";

import fr.code_civil.contrat version "0.1.0";
import fr.code_civil.core version "0.1.0";
import fr.code_civil.transitions version "0.1.0";

// ONE LONG-TERM CONTRACT, TWO TRACKS OF ONE CRISIS.
//
// The same supply contract concluded on 1 March 2017 (after the 1 October
// 2016 corridor) is read stage by stage. On the left, article 1195:
// renegotiation, the duty to perform during it, then the court. On the
// right, article 1218: suspension, termination by operation of law.
// The model does not adapt the contract; it opens the right to apply to
// the court. Unforeseeability, excessive onerousness, reasonable time,
// reasonable foreseeability and unavoidable effects are the court's
// findings (DECISION-0194). No norm is written here.
